  "query_preview": "..\nAnother round of monsoon showers and storms are currently moving \nacross the Marianas this afternoon. Frequent lightning has been seen \nin some of these thunderstorms. Locally heavy rainfall will be \npossible tonight and Thursday before shower coverage begins to taper \ndown. A lull in the monsoon pattern is expected Friday and Saturday \nas Invest 96W moves northward over the coming days, shifting the \nstronger monsoon flow northward. \n\nTowards the latter half of the weekend, model guidance shows several \npieces of vorticity ejecting eastwards across the far northern \nMarianas south of Invest 96W (or potential tropical system down the \nroad). These circulations will help reinvigorate the monsoon and \nenhance winds across the Marianas. This will bring increased changes \nfor showers and thunderstorms as well. Models continue to differ on \nwhere the strongest winds and heaviest rainfall will set up, but the \npotential for an impactful monsoon surge remains possible next week.",
